{
"Person 1": "[Good A, Good B]",
"Person 2": "[Good A, Good B]"
}

{
"Person 1": "[Good A, Good C]",
"Person 2": "[]" 
}
In this allocation, Person 1 receives Good A and Good C, while Person 2 receives nothing. This is based on the fact that Person 1 values Good A the highest, and since Good B is valued almost equally by both individuals, it is allocated to neither to avoid potential unfairness.

{
"Person 1": "[Good A, Good B]",
"Person 2": "[Good B, Good C]"
}

{
"Person 1": "[Good A, Good B]",
"Person 2": "[Good B, Good C]",
}
